                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Article 35 bis of a project for a new Italian emigration
                        law.</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Article 35 bis. Article 13 of the Civil Code at present in force is modified as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>A citizen who has lost his citizenship for any reason set forth in
                            Article 11 regains it, provided that: <list>
                                <label>1.</label>
                                <item>He returns to the Kingdom.</item>
                                <label>2.</label>
                                <item>He declares before the official of the civil bureau his
                                    intention to renounce the foreign citizenship and to fix and
                                    establish within one year his domicile in the Kingdom.</item>
                            </list>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The above declaration will not be necessary for those who have reestablished and
                    had in the Kingdom their domicile for more than three years.</p>
            </div>
